    "built_to": "deliver a reliable byte stream over an unreliable internet using windows and retransmission timers",
    "pressure": "packet loss and delay from shared links; but the design did not yet read loss as a congestion signal",
    "success_means": "data arrives in order; when the network is congested this version keeps retransmitting into it -- the human record marks that as its failure"
  },
  "known_human_problem_solved": "reliable transport (without congestion control)",
  "hardware_assumptions": "",
  "human_environmental_pressure": "bandwidth scarcity on shared links, packet loss, queueing delay",
